  "title": "Separability",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "27850fe4-971f-40fb-a52a-581f54eec315",
      "text": "Two systems are separable when their joint state factors into individual states, so they have zero entanglement entropy and can be measured independently. Separable states are decoherent, entangled states coherent.",
